course: dictionary
lesson: 15474
title: Stranded: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stranded means stuck in a place and unable to leave. «Our train was cancelled, so we were stranded at the station for three hours.» The clue is cancelled: with no train, the children could not go anywhere.
explain: Stranded can also describe an animal or boat. «The young whale was stranded on the beach, too weak to swim back to the sea.» The clues are beach and swim back to the sea, so stranded means left somewhere it cannot get out of.
explain: Something made of strands, which are threads twisted together, can also be stranded. «The electric cable had a stranded copper core.» Here the clue is the word cable, so stranded means made of twisted threads. Always check the words around it: they tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Stranded means stuck in a place and cannot leave.
fact: «Stranded» can also mean a whale, fish or boat left on a beach or in shallow water, unable to get back to the sea.
fact: «Stranded» can describe a cable made of strands, which are threads twisted together.
fact: Phrases to know: stranded on an island, left stranded, stranded at the airport.
fact: If you are stranded, stay together, call for help and keep warm.
exercise: «The snow closed the roads, and the travellers were stranded in the village.» What does stranded mean here? | Happy and free to go | Very wet | Made of threads twisted together | *Stuck and unable to leave
exercise: «The tired seal was stranded on the sand, far from the sea.» Which meaning fits best? | Swimming fast in the sea | Singing a happy song on the rocks | Asleep in a warm bed | *Left on the beach, unable to get back to the sea
exercise: Mia reads, «If you are stranded in the hills, stay together and call for help.» What should you do if you are stranded? | *Stay together, call for help and keep warm | Split up and go in different directions | Hide your phone in your bag
test:  «Our train was cancelled, so we were stranded at the station.» What does stranded mean? | Floating on the water | Early for the train | Very excited | *Stuck and unable to leave
test: «The cable was stranded, made of many thin wires twisted together.» What does stranded mean here? | Left on a beach | Stuck in a place | *Made of strands twisted together | Lost in the sea
exam: Which sentence uses stranded to mean a boat or animal left on a beach? | «The stranded cable was made of six twisted threads.» | *«The boat was stranded on the sand when the tide went out.» | «She was stranded at the airport all night.»
